{"questions":[{"question_id":"jaoe38c1lsd39r8j","content":"<p>The number of ways in which 21 identical apples can be distributed among three children such that each child gets at least 2 apples, is</p>","chapter":"permutations-and-combinations","chapterGroup":"algebra","country":"in","difficulty":"medium","exam":"jee-main","examGroup":"jee","languages":["en","hi"],"marks":4,"negMarks":1,"paperId":"jee-main-2024-online-31st-january-evening-shift","paperTitle":"JEE Main 2024 (Online) 31st January Evening Shift","permalink":"pthe-number-of-ways-in-which-21-identical-apples-can-be-di-jee-main-mathematics-trigonometric-functions-and-equations-3irksefr8i9et9de","question":{"en":{"comprehension":null,"direction":null,"content":"<p>The number of ways in which 21 identical apples can be distributed among three children such that each child gets at least 2 apples, is</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"130"},{"identifier":"B","content":"136"},{"identifier":"C","content":"142"},{"identifier":"D","content":"406"}],"correct_options":["B"],"answer":null,"explanation":"<p>To solve this problem, we can use a classic combinatorics method known as \"stars and bars\" (or \"balls and bins\"), which is a way to solve problems involving distributing identical items into distinct groups with certain restrictions.</p>\n\n<p>First, since each child must get at least 2 apples, let's give 2 apples to each child right away. That accounts for 6 apples (2 apples for each of the 3 children). Now, we have 21 - 6 = 15 apples left to distribute freely among the three children.</p>\n\n<p>The \"stars and bars\" technique involves representing the apples as stars (*) and the divisions between children as bars (|). For example, if we had 5 apples to distribute among three children, one possible distribution could be represented as **|*|**. This means the first child gets 2 apples, the second child gets 1 apple, and the third child gets 2 apples.</p>\n\n<p>In our case, we need to distribute 15 apples (stars) among the three children with 2 bars to create the partitions. We arrange 15 stars and 2 bars in a row, where the arrangement of stars and bars corresponds to a distribution of the apples.</p>\n\n<p>The total number of objects we're arranging is 15 apples + 2 bars = 17 objects. We need to choose 2 positions out of these 17 to place the bars. The remaining positions will be occupied by the stars (apples).</p>\n\n<p>The number of ways to choose 2 positions out of 17 for the bars is given by the binomial coefficient:</p>\n\n<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -1.469ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"51.781ex\" height=\"4.07ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -1149.5 22887.3 1799\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mtext\" style=\"font-family: Roboto,'Tiro Devanagari Hindi','Tiro Bangla',sans-serif;\"><text data-variant=\"-explicitFont\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\" font-size=\"884px\">Number of ways</text></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(8677.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mrow\" transform=\"translate(9733.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"OPEN\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(0 -0.5)\"><use data-c=\"28\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-LO-28\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mfrac\" transform=\"translate(597,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(0,444) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use><use data-c=\"37\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-37\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(176.8,-345) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"CLOSE\" transform=\"translate(1304.1,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(0 -0.5)\"><use data-c=\"29\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-LO-29\"></use></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(11912.4,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mfrac\" transform=\"translate(12968.2,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mrow\" transform=\"translate(1222,394) scale(0.707)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use><use data-c=\"37\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-37\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1000,0)\"><use data-c=\"21\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-21\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mrow\" transform=\"translate(220,-370.3) scale(0.707)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"><use data-c=\"21\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-21\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(778,0)\"><use data-c=\"28\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-28\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1167,0)\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use><use data-c=\"37\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-37\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(2167,0)\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(2945,0)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(3445,0)\"><use data-c=\"29\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-29\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(3834,0)\"><use data-c=\"21\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-21\"></use></g></g><rect width=\"3107.6\" height=\"60\" x=\"120\" y=\"220\"></rect></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(16593.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mfrac\" transform=\"translate(17649.4,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mrow\" transform=\"translate(220,394) scale(0.707)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use><use data-c=\"37\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-37\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1000,0)\"><use data-c=\"D7\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-D7\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1778,0)\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use><use data-c=\"36\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-36\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mrow\" transform=\"translate(573.6,-345) scale(0.707)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"><use data-c=\"D7\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-D7\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1278,0)\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use></g></g><rect width=\"2164.3\" height=\"60\" x=\"120\" y=\"220\"></rect></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(20331.5,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(21387.3,0)\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"></use><use data-c=\"36\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-36\" transform=\"translate(1000,0)\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>\n\n<p>Thus, there are 136 ways to distribute the 21 identical apples among three children such that each child gets at least 2 apples. The correct answer is Option B: 136.</p>"},"hi":{"direction":null,"comprehension":null,"content":"<p>21 सर्वसम सेव को तीन बच्चों में बाँटने के तरीकों, जब की प्रत्येक बच्चे को कम से कम दो सेव मिलें, की संख्या है।</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"130"},{"identifier":"B","content":"136"},{"identifier":"C","content":"142"},{"identifier":"D","content":"406"}],"correct_options":["B"],"answer":null,"explanation":"<p>इस समस्या को हल करने के लिए, हम एक क्लासिक संयोजन विधि का उपयोग कर सकते हैं जिसे \"stars and bars\" (या \"balls and bins\") के नाम से जाना जाता है, जो कि निश्चित प्रतिबंधों के साथ समान वस्तुओं को भिन्न समूहों में वितरित करने से संबंधित समस्याओं को हल करने का एक तरीका है।</p>\n\n<p>सबसे पहले, चूंकि प्रत्येक बच्चे को कम से कम 2 सेब मिलने चाहिए, तो आइए तुरंत प्रत्येक बच्चे को 2 सेब दे दें। इससे 6 सेब (3 बच्चों में से प्रत्येक के लिए 2 सेब) का हिसाब हो जाता है। अब, हमारे पास तीन बच्चों के बीच स्वतंत्र रूप से वितरित करने के लिए 21 - 6 = 15 सेब बचे हैं।</p>\n\n<p>\"Stars and bars\" तकनीक में सेब को तारों (*) के रूप में और बच्चों के बीच विभाजन को bars (|) के रूप में दर्शाया जाता है। उदाहरण के लिए, यदि हमारे पास तीन बच्चों के बीच वितरित करने के लिए 5 सेब हों, तो एक संभावित वितरण को **|*|** के रूप में दर्शाया जा सकता है। इसका अर्थ है कि पहले बच्चे को 2 सेब, दूसरे बच्चे को 1 सेब, और तीसरे बच्चे को 2 सेब मिलते हैं।</p>\n\n<p>हमारे मामले में, हमें 15 सेब (stars) को तीन बच्चों के बीच 2 bars के साथ वितरित करने की आवश्यकता है ताकि विभाजन बन सकें। हम 15 stars और 2 bars को एक पंक्ति में व्यवस्थित करते हैं, जहां stars और bars की व्यवस्था सेबों के वितरण से संबंधित है।</p>\n\n<p>हम जो कुल वस्तुएं व्यवस्थित कर रहे हैं वे हैं 15 सेब + 2 bars = 17 वस्तुएं। हमें bars रखने के लिए इन 17 में से 2 स्थान चुनने की आवश्यकता है। शेष स्थान stars (सेब) द्वारा अधिकृत होंगे।</p>\n\n<p>Bars के लिए 17 में से 2 स्थान चुनने के तरीकों की संख्या द्विपद गुणांक द्वारा दी जाती है:</p>\n\n<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -1.469ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"54.496ex\" height=\"4.07ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -1149.5 24087.3 1799\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mtext\" style=\"font-family: Roboto,'Tiro Devanagari Hindi','Tiro Bangla',sans-serif;\"><text data-variant=\"-explicitFont\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\" font-size=\"884px\">तरीकों की संख्या</text></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(9877.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mrow\" transform=\"translate(10933.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"OPEN\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(0 -0.5)\"><use data-c=\"28\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-LO-28\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mfrac\" transform=\"translate(597,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(0,444) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use><use data-c=\"37\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-37\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(176.8,-345) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"CLOSE\" transform=\"translate(1304.1,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(0 -0.5)\"><use data-c=\"29\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-LO-29\"></use></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(13112.4,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mfrac\" transform=\"translate(14168.2,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mrow\" transform=\"translate(1222,394) scale(0.707)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use><use data-c=\"37\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-37\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1000,0)\"><use data-c=\"21\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-21\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mrow\" transform=\"translate(220,-370.3) scale(0.707)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"><use data-c=\"21\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-21\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(778,0)\"><use data-c=\"28\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-28\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1167,0)\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use><use data-c=\"37\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-37\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(2167,0)\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(2945,0)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(3445,0)\"><use data-c=\"29\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-29\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(3834,0)\"><use data-c=\"21\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-21\"></use></g></g><rect width=\"3107.6\" height=\"60\" x=\"120\" y=\"220\"></rect></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(17793.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mfrac\" transform=\"translate(18849.4,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mrow\" transform=\"translate(220,394) scale(0.707)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use><use data-c=\"37\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-37\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1000,0)\"><use data-c=\"D7\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-D7\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1778,0)\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use><use data-c=\"36\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-36\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mrow\" transform=\"translate(573.6,-345) scale(0.707)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"><use data-c=\"D7\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-D7\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1278,0)\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use></g></g><rect width=\"2164.3\" height=\"60\" x=\"120\" y=\"220\"></rect></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(21531.5,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(22587.3,0)\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"></use><use data-c=\"36\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-36\" transform=\"translate(1000,0)\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>\n\n<p>इस प्रकार, 21 समान सेबों को तीन बच्चों के बीच इस प्रकार वितरित करने के 136 तरीके हैं कि प्रत्येक बच्चे को कम से कम 2 सेब मिलें। सही उत्तर विकल्प B: 136 है।</p>"}},"subject":"mathematics","subjectGroup":null,"timeAllotted":120000,"topic":"conditional-combinations","type":"mcq","year":2024,"isOutOfSyllabus":false,"isBonus":false,"tags":[],"yearKey":"jee-main-2024-online-31st-january-evening-shift","active":true,"options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"130"},{"identifier":"B","content":"136"},{"identifier":"C","content":"142"},{"identifier":"D","content":"406"}],"correct_options":["B"],"explanation":"<p>To solve this problem, we can use a classic combinatorics method known as \"stars and bars\" (or \"balls and bins\"), which is a way to solve problems involving distributing identical items into distinct groups with certain restrictions.</p>\n\n<p>First, since each child must get at least 2 apples, let's give 2 apples to each child right away. That accounts for 6 apples (2 apples for each of the 3 children). Now, we have 21 - 6 = 15 apples left to distribute freely among the three children.</p>\n\n<p>The \"stars and bars\" technique involves representing the apples as stars (*) and the divisions between children as bars (|). For example, if we had 5 apples to distribute among three children, one possible distribution could be represented as **|*|**. This means the first child gets 2 apples, the second child gets 1 apple, and the third child gets 2 apples.</p>\n\n<p>In our case, we need to distribute 15 apples (stars) among the three children with 2 bars to create the partitions. We arrange 15 stars and 2 bars in a row, where the arrangement of stars and bars corresponds to a distribution of the apples.</p>\n\n<p>The total number of objects we're arranging is 15 apples + 2 bars = 17 objects. We need to choose 2 positions out of these 17 to place the bars. The remaining positions will be occupied by the stars (apples).</p>\n\n<p>The number of ways to choose 2 positions out of 17 for the bars is given by the binomial coefficient:</p>\n\n<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -1.469ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"51.781ex\" height=\"4.07ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -1149.5 22887.3 1799\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mtext\" style=\"font-family: Roboto,'Tiro Devanagari Hindi','Tiro Bangla',sans-serif;\"><text data-variant=\"-explicitFont\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\" font-size=\"884px\">Number of ways</text></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(8677.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mrow\" transform=\"translate(9733.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"OPEN\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(0 -0.5)\"><use data-c=\"28\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-LO-28\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mfrac\" transform=\"translate(597,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(0,444) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use><use data-c=\"37\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-37\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(176.8,-345) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"CLOSE\" transform=\"translate(1304.1,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(0 -0.5)\"><use data-c=\"29\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-LO-29\"></use></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(11912.4,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mfrac\" transform=\"translate(12968.2,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mrow\" transform=\"translate(1222,394) scale(0.707)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use><use data-c=\"37\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-37\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1000,0)\"><use data-c=\"21\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-21\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mrow\" transform=\"translate(220,-370.3) scale(0.707)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"><use data-c=\"21\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-21\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(778,0)\"><use data-c=\"28\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-28\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1167,0)\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use><use data-c=\"37\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-37\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(2167,0)\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(2945,0)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(3445,0)\"><use data-c=\"29\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-29\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(3834,0)\"><use data-c=\"21\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-21\"></use></g></g><rect width=\"3107.6\" height=\"60\" x=\"120\" y=\"220\"></rect></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(16593.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mfrac\" transform=\"translate(17649.4,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mrow\" transform=\"translate(220,394) scale(0.707)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use><use data-c=\"37\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-37\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1000,0)\"><use data-c=\"D7\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-D7\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1778,0)\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use><use data-c=\"36\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-36\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mrow\" transform=\"translate(573.6,-345) scale(0.707)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"><use data-c=\"D7\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-D7\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1278,0)\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use></g></g><rect width=\"2164.3\" height=\"60\" x=\"120\" y=\"220\"></rect></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(20331.5,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(21387.3,0)\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"></use><use data-c=\"36\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-36\" transform=\"translate(1000,0)\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>\n\n<p>Thus, there are 136 ways to distribute the 21 identical apples among three children such that each child gets at least 2 apples. The correct answer is Option B: 136.</p>"}]}